      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we keep the explicit `reserved` byte? Without it, the structure remains four bytes only because of tail padding. The ESP designated initializers initialize the three named bytes, but the compiler need not initialize that padding—GCC 13 at `-O2` leaves it untouched. Since `vlib_buffer_get_next_frame_with_aux64_and_scalar()` compares and copies all four bytes, logically identical metadata may compare unequal and prematurely dispatch a partial frame, defeating batching. The explicit member ensures every compared byte is initialized.",
      "revId": "89fa4abd116a39b35380a15fa2bf957aa472f337",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
